(Bug #64: no Number Properties row parsed behind the article, and the
 two spellings disagreed in both directions - a quoted multi-word timer
 property (`t's 'start time'`) parsed only WITH the article, while every
 number property parsed only without it. One property-resolution path
 now, so both spellings read both.)

a number called depth is -7.
Print "absolute: {the depth's absolute}".
Print "sign: {the depth's sign}".
Print "even: {the depth's even}".
Print "odd: {the depth's odd}".
Print "positive: {the depth's positive}".
Print "negative: {the depth's negative}".
Print "zero: {the depth's zero}".

a number called nought is 0.
Print "zero of 0: {the nought's zero}".

Create a timer called 'job timer'.
Start the 'job timer'.
Stop the 'job timer'.

Print "running: {the 'job timer''s running}".

(`start time` as two words and `'start time'` as one quoted name are the
 same property, and the article does not change which one is read.)
If 'job timer''s start time is equal to the 'job timer''s start time then,
    Print "start time: agree".
If 'job timer''s 'start time' is equal to the 'job timer''s 'start time' then,
    Print "quoted start time: agree".
If 'job timer''s 'end time' is equal to the 'job timer''s end time then,
    Print "end time: agree across spellings".
